FUNCTION UNDER TEST:
Name: process_guess
Signature: int process_guess(struct game_instance *game, char guess)
Description: /**
 * @brief Process a single letter guess in a word-guessing game.
 *
 * Validates the guess, records it, and updates the game state. The guess is
 * converted to lowercase. If the letter is in the target word, it is revealed
 * in the hidden word representation; otherwise, the incorrect guess count is
 * incremented.
 *
 * @param game Pointer to the game instance structure. Must not be NULL.
 * @param guess The letter being guessed.
 *
 * @return 1 if the guess is correct (letter is in the word),
 *         0 if the guess is incorrect,
 *         -1 on error (NULL game or duplicate guess).
 *
 * @note Modifies the `guesses` array, `guesses_size`, `hidden` array, and
 *       `incorrect` counter within the game instance.
 * @note The guess is stored in the guesses array only if there is space
 *       (array size < 25).
 *
 * @see in_word, new_guess
 */
Dependencies: in_word, new_guess

FUNCTION IMPLEMENTATION (REFERENCE ONLY - do NOT copy into test):
```c
// C program for the function called process_guess
// Contains target function implementation and dependency signatures

#include <ctype.h> /// for tolower()
#include <stdio.h> /// for I/O operations
#include <stdlib.h> /// for exit(), rand() and memory functions
#include <string.h> /// for string operations strlen, strchr, strcpy
#include <time.h> /// for srand()
#include "header.h"

// Forward declarations for dependency functions
int new_guess(char new_guess, const char guesses[], int size);
int in_word(char letter, const char word[], int size);

// Target function implementation
int process_guess(struct game_instance *game, char guess) {
    if (game == NULL) {
        return -1;
    }

    guess = tolower(guess);

    // Check if already guessed
    if (new_guess(guess, game->guesses, game->guesses_size) != -1) {
        return -1; // Already guessed
    }

    // Add to guesses array
    if (game->guesses_size < 25) {
        game->guesses[game->guesses_size] = guess;
        game->guesses_size++;
    }

    // Check if letter is in word
    if (in_word(guess, game->current_word, game->size) == 1) {
        // Reveal the letter in hidden
        for (int i = 0; i < game->size; i++) {
            if (tolower(game->current_word[i]) == guess) {
                game->hidden[i] = game->current_word[i];
            }
        }
        return 1; // Correct guess
    } else {
        game->incorrect++;
        return 0; // Incorrect guess
    }
}

```

